anics","subchapterId":"8.1","subchapterTitle":"8.1 Constructing a model","number":"7","question":"<span class=\"practice-tag\">P</span> The model for the motion of Rashid&#x27;s shot given in question 3 is only valid when <span data-math=\"h\"></span> is positive.\n<ol type=\"a\"><li value=\"1\">Find the range of values of <span data-math=\"x\"></span> for which the model is valid.</li><li value=\"2\">Work out the maximum height of Rashid&#x27;s shot above his chest.</li></ol>\nWhen Sam takes a throw in the shot put, the motion of the shot can be modelled using the equation <span data-math=\"h=0.6x-0.04x^2\"></span>, where <span data-math=\"h\"></span> m is the height of the shot above his chest and <span data-math=\"x\"></span> m is the horizontal distance travelled. The player that throws the shot furthest wins the competition.\n<ol type=\"a\"><li value=\"1\">Use the models given to determine who will win the contest, and find the distance by which they win. Assume the shot finishes at the same height as it started in each case.</li></ol>","hints":[],"steps":[],"solutionStatus":"pending","skillIds":[],"topicIds":[],"source":{"kind":"practice-booklet","pdf":"resources/practice/applied-year-1/chapter-08.pdf","pdfSha256":"9d8ef6696b7c62a15bf8354eae27ac596ce9a69fc6ac6a2bec4036e918148b84","nativeSha256":"38d6c6a4a898c01cef255fecfd79e5b385c5fbba288c8aea8ce328cda90450b8","questionLatexSha256":"75a2e3dfe9e7403cade03ea2f0d822697d7ae394cc97f610b810ab1397c620a4","printedBookPage":"52","marker":{"page":3,"bbox":[58.494,263.072,68.247,273.981]},"coordinateSystem":"PDF points, top-left origin","extraction":"native-latex","boundaryCheck":"all printed question markers match native sequence"}},{"id":"practice/maths-a-level/maths-mechanics-year-1/ch8/8.1/q8","courseId":"maths-a-level","bookId":"maths-mechanics-year-1","chapterId":"ch8","chapterNumber":8,"questionLabel":"8","chapterTitle":"Modelling in mechanics","subchapterId":"8.1","subchapterTitle":"8.1 Constructing a model","number":"8","question":"<span class=\"practice-tag\">E/P</span>  The motion of a netball as it leaves a player&#x27;s hand and passes through the net is modelled using the equation <span data-math=\"h=1.8+1.2x-0.2x^2\"></span>, where <span data-math=\"h\"></span> m is the height of the netball above the ground and <span data-math=\"x\"></span> m is the horizontal distance travelled.\n<ol type=\"a\"><li value=\"1\">Write down the height of the ball when it leaves the player&#x27;s hand. <span class=\"marks\">(1 mark)</span></li><li value=\"2\">Find the two values of <span data-math=\"x\"></span> for which the netball is exactly 3.4 m above the ground. <span class=\"marks\">(2 marks)</span></li></ol>\nThe model is only valid for <span data-math=\"0\\le x\\le k\"></span>, where <span data-math=\"k\"></span> m is the horizontal distance of the net from the player. Given that the height of the net is 2.8 m and that the netball passes through the net as it is travelling downwards:\n<ol type=\"a\"><li value=\"1\">find the range of values of <span data-math=\"x\"></span> for which the model is valid <span class=\"marks\">(1 mark)</span></li><li value=\"2\">work out the maximum height of the netball. <span class=\"marks\">(2 marks)</span></li></ol>","hints":[],"steps":[],"solutionStatus":"pending","skillIds":[],"topicIds":[],"source":{"kind":"practice-booklet","pdf":"resources/practice/applied-year-1/chapter-08.pdf","pdfSha256":"9d8ef6696b7c62a15bf8354eae27ac596ce9a69fc6ac6a2bec4036e918148b84","nativeSha256":"38d6c6a4a898c01cef255fecfd79e5b385c5fbba288c8aea8ce328cda90450b8","questionLatexSha256":"983f47b8050477f6e95afb27fdd254a4a6936bfd96e77dd0ba4c8d4d46ed4119","printedBookPage":"52","marker":{"page":3,"bbox":[58.494,387.406,68.247,398.315]},"coordinateSystem":"PDF points, top-left origin","extraction":"native-latex","boundaryCheck":"all printed question markers match native sequence"}},{"id":"practice/maths-a-level/maths-mechanics-year-1/ch8/8.2/q1","courseId":"maths-a-level",