\"></span></li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(3 marks)</span></li><li value=\"2\">Use the model to predict the height of the ball when <span data-math=\"x=10\"></span>.\nComment on the validity of this prediction. <span class=\"marks\">(2 marks)</span></li></ol>","hints":[],"steps":[],"solutionStatus":"pending","skillIds":[],"topicIds":[],"source":{"kind":"practice-booklet","pdf":"resources/practice/applied-year-1/chapter-08.pdf","pdfSha256":"9d8ef6696b7c62a15bf8354eae27ac596ce9a69fc6ac6a2bec4036e918148b84","nativeSha256":"38d6c6a4a898c01cef255fecfd79e5b385c5fbba288c8aea8ce328cda90450b8","questionLatexSha256":"ba8f7ce788203f1a6908d2f31e21be8bb555e9243fc5a4d4b2425dbc5b38fcdf","printedBookPage":"55","marker":{"page":8,"bbox":[57.49,70.959,92.797,80.922]},"coordinateSystem":"PDF points, top-left origin","extraction":"native-latex","boundaryCheck":"all printed question markers match native sequence"}},{"id":"practice/maths-a-level/maths-mechanics-year-1/ch8/problem-a/qsilver","courseId":"maths-a-level","bookId":"maths-mechanics-year-1","chapterId":"ch8","chapterNumber":8,"questionLabel":"Silver","chapterTitle":"Modelling in mechanics","subchapterId":"problem-a","subchapterTitle":"Problem set A","number":"Silver","question":"The motion of a volleyball after it is served by a player is modelled using the equation <span data-math=\"h=1.2+x-0.2x^2\"></span>, where <span data-math=\"h\"></span> m is the height of the volleyball above the ground and <span data-math=\"x\"></span> m is the horizontal distance travelled.\n<ol type=\"a\"><li value=\"1\">Write down the height of the ball when it leaves the player&#x27;s hand. <span class=\"marks\">(1 mark)</span></li></ol>\nThe model for the motion of a volleyball is only valid when <span data-math=\"h\"></span> is positive.\n<ol type=\"a\"><li value=\"2\">Find the range of values of <span data-math=\"x\"></span> for which the model is valid. <span class=\"marks\">(2 marks)</span></li><li value=\"3\">A player stands <span data-math=\